## SQ-RD-10b | plains village farms unchanged by the warm_dry rule: no cotton (plains half of SQ-RD-10)
> locate structure minecraft:village_plains
waitlog The nearest minecraft:village_plains 600
capture VP The nearest minecraft:village_plains is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> forceload add {VP1-48} {VP3-48} {VP1+48} {VP3+48}
sleep 40
> zq count {VP1-56} 40 {VP3-56} {VP1+56} 160 {VP3+56} minecraft:wheat
waitlog \[zq\] count minecraft:wheat 300
> zq count {VP1-56} 40 {VP3-56} {VP1+56} 160 {VP3+56} minecraft:carrots
> zq count {VP1-56} 40 {VP3-56} {VP1+56} 160 {VP3+56} minecraft:potatoes
> zq count {VP1-56} 40 {VP3-56} {VP1+56} 160 {VP3+56} minecraft:beetroots
> zq count {VP1-56} 40 {VP3-56} {VP1+56} 160 {VP3+56} rusticdelight:cotton
waitlog \[zq\] count rusticdelight:cotton 300
expect \[zq\] count minecraft:(wheat|carrots|potatoes|beetroots): [1-9]
expect \[zq\] count rusticdelight:cotton: 0;
look plains crops present (the box hit the village); temperate crops (cabbage, onion, tomato...) may replace some fields, cotton never

## SQ-WCD-07 | savanna village farms: cotton among the warm_dry replacements; the cotton biome tag
> zq biometag creativedelight:wild_crops/cotton
expect biometag creativedelight:wild_crops/cotton \(\d+\): .*minecraft:savanna
look the three savanna cotton counts are in rows/SQ-RD-10.log; cotton is about 3% of fields, so 0 in three villages is not a fail when SQ-RD-10 shows other warm_dry crops (farm crops are chosen by template group, village_farms.json, not by this tag: the row text is stale)

## SQ-WCD-02 | jungle: cocoa and melons; beach: wild cabbages on sand (second jungle and beach away from spawn)
> zq biometag creativedelight:wild_crops/melon
> zq biometag creativedelight:wild_crops/cabbage
expect biometag creativedelight:wild_crops/melon \(\d+\): .*minecraft:jungle
expect biometag creativedelight:wild_crops/cabbage \(\d+\): .*minecraft:beach
> execute positioned 2500 70 -2500 run locate biome minecraft:jungle
waitlog The nearest minecraft:jungle 600
capture JG The nearest minecraft:jungle is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> forceload add {JG1-48} {JG3-48} {JG1+48} {JG3+48}
sleep 40
> zq count {JG1-56} 40 {JG3-56} {JG1+56} 200 {JG3+56} minecraft:cocoa
waitlog \[zq\] count minecraft:cocoa 300
> zq count {JG1-56} 40 {JG3-56} {JG1+56} 200 {JG3+56} minecraft:melon
waitlog \[zq\] count minecraft:melon 300
expect \[zq\] count minecraft:cocoa: [1-9]
expect \[zq\] count minecraft:melon: [1-9]
> execute positioned 2500 70 2500 run locate biome minecraft:beach
waitlog The nearest minecraft:beach 600
capture BC The nearest minecraft:beach is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> forceload add {BC1-48} {BC3-48} {BC1+48} {BC3+48}
sleep 40
> zq count {BC1-56} 50 {BC3-56} {BC1+56} 100 {BC3+56} minecraft:sand
waitlog \[zq\] count minecraft:sand 300
> zq count {BC1-56} 50 {BC3-56} {BC1+56} 100 {BC3+56} farmersdelight:wild_cabbages
waitlog \[zq\] count farmersdelight:wild_cabbages 300
expect \[zq\] count farmersdelight:wild_cabbages: [1-9]\d*; on: .*minecraft:sand
look 7 x 7 chunks per biome (jungle near 2500 -2500, beach near 2500 2500); the sand count shows how much beach the box holds: a 0 cabbage count on a few hundred sand blocks is weak evidence, on thousands a fail

